Model parameters were established using empirical statistical data (2021–2025) from Statistics Indonesia (BPS) and the Regional Department of Agriculture in East Java. Empirical variables—including agricultural land area (ALA = 1,841,346 ha), birth rate (BR = 0.01320 year
− 1
), mortality rate (MR = 0.00788 year
− 1
), and baseline chemical fertilizer usage (CFU = 1,723,682 tons/year) were parameterized directly from historical records.

A causal loop diagram (CLD) is used to map the feedback structure of a sustainable rice food security system based on TBL aspects. Standard conventions for constructing a CLD [27], [28], [29] include: 1) arrows indicate the direction of the relationship from cause (upstream) to effect (downstream); 2) a positive symbol ($+
